/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 805 0 R
/T (Fully Homomorphic Encryption \(FHE\) provides a powerful framework for preserving the privacy of sensitive data by enabling computations directly on encrypted data. However, developing efficient FHE programs presents significant challenges, including noise management, vectorization, and performance optimization. Equality saturation emerges as a promising technique to address these challenges by enabling systematic and efficient vectorization of FHE code. This study explores state-of-art FHE compliers and current applications of Equality saturation.)
/E (Fully Homomorphic Encryption \(FHE\) provides a powerful framework for preserving the privacy of sensitive data by enabling computations directly on encrypted data. However, developing efficient FHE programs presents significant challenges, including noise management, vectorization, and performance optimization. Equality saturation emerges as a promising technique to address these challenges by enabling systematic and efficient vectorization of FHE code. This study explores state-of-art FHE compliers and current applications of Equality saturation.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [46]
>>
endobj
983 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 805 0 R
/T (In recent years, the growing reliance on cloud-based data processing has raised serious concerns about the privacy of sensitive information, such as health and financial data. Fully Homomorphic Encryption \(FHE\) offers a strong cryptographic solution by enabling computations to be performed directly on encrypted data. While FHE provides strong security guarantees, it remains computationally demanding, making its an active area for practical deployment.)
/E (In recent years, the growing reliance on cloud-based data processing has raised serious concerns about the privacy of sensitive information, such as health and financial data. Fully Homomorphic Encryption \(FHE\) offers a strong cryptographic solution by enabling computations to be performed directly on encrypted data. While FHE provides strong security guarantees, it remains computationally demanding, making its an active area for practical deployment.)
/Pg 10 0 R
