<<
/Title (Scalability: Equality saturation can lead to large e-graphs, making it memory and time-intensive, especially for complex FHE circuits.)
/Dest [9 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4264 0 R
/Next 4465 0 R
>>
endobj
4390 0 obj
<<
/Title (Hybrid Approaches: Combining equality saturation with greedy or heuristic methods could balance exploration and performance.)
/Dest [9 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4264 0 R
/Prev 4465 0 R
>>
endobj
4391 0 obj
<<
/Title (Fully Homomorphic Encryption \(FHE\) provides a powerful framework for preserving the privacy of sensitive data by enabling computations directly on encrypted data. However, developing efficient FHE programs presents significant challenges, including noise management, vectorization, and performance optimization. Equality saturation emerges as a promising technique to address these challenges by enabling systematic and efficient vectorization of FHE code. This study explores state-of-art FHE compliers and current applications of Equality saturation.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4266 0 R
/Next 4392 0 R
>>
endobj
4392 0 obj
<<
/Title (Key words : Fully Homomorphic Encryption, Equality saturation, Automatic code optimization, Vectorization)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4266 0 R
/Prev 4391 0 R
>>
