4569 0 obj
<<
/Title (CHEHAB is a compiler for FHE that automatically optimizes code by minimizing noise growth and circuit latency. It introduces a DSL embedded in C++ to abstract FHE concepts and allow developer to write high-level code without managing FHE operations. The compilation pipeline begins by lowering the DSL into an intermediate representation \(IR\), followed by two optimization passes: the first uses an equality saturation-based term rewriting system \(TRS\) to perform vectorization, and the second applies a greedy TRS to reduce noise growth by simplifying arithmetic expressions.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 4551 0 R
>>
endobj
